ritual of closure mark the end of this journey with a symbolic act:
<break time="600ms"/>
light a candle and say aloud: “i set down what was never.
<break time="600ms"/>
mine to carry.”
<break time="600ms"/>
write “i resign from being the eldest daughter role” and burn it.
<break time="600ms"/>
take yourself on a graduation date: flowers, dinner, a walk, a gift.
<break time="600ms"/>
what would it feel like to finally graduate from the eldest daughter role remember this...
<break time="600ms"/>
you never stopped needing play. you just learned to bury it. joy is not childish: it’s medicine. every laugh, every silly moment, every act of rest tells your nervous system: i am safe now. i get to live too.
<break time="600ms"/>
</speak>
